# Compiled circuit / verifier artifacts are generated blobs, not source.
#
# `-diff` (and the `binary` macro it comes from) tells git to emit
# "Binary files a/… and b/… differ" instead of the file contents, which is what
# you want for these anyway: the ACIR JSON is one 3 MB line with no newlines, so
# a normal diff is a single unreadable `+` line, and the Solidity verifier is
# 2700 lines of generated field constants.
#
# The side effect that matters: .husky/pre-commit greps the staged diff for
# secret-shaped hex (`0x?[a-f0-9]{64}`) and these artifacts are full of
# legitimate matches — BN254 field constants and the Aztec verification-key
# hash. There is no way to annotate them with the hook's `// nosec: <reason>`
# escape (it would corrupt the JSON, and the .sol has 62 matching lines). With
# no diff content to scan, the hook sees nothing and the real secret scan is
# left untouched for every other file.
#
# Scoped to these exact paths on purpose — do NOT broaden this to `*.json`.
assets/circuits/registerIdentity_*.json -diff
circuits/*.sol                          -diff
circuits/*.vk                           -diff binary
